 in which case it's safe\n- Throw a NumberFormatException (if it's not numeric), which is handled by the catch block\nThe parameterized query approach properly separates the SQL structure from user-supplied values, preventing injection attacks. Beyond SQL injection, I should consider other potential issues like whether the code properly validates access permissions before deleting records, and whether exposing the number of affected rows could leak sensitive information about the database state.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":33939,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a04ddb5-d2dc-4a27-8763-dbf60e54a432","uuid":"802e9672-1070-4158-a4c8-e8f717e10a83","timestamp":"2026-07-24T19:37:29.456Z","request_id":"req_vrtx_011CdMSqUef3mbqNv1tq4ncw"}
